.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-ZFS-DBGMSG-COLLECTOR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-zfs-dbgmsg-collector
.Nd copy new ZFS debug messages into a log the metrics stack can read
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The ZFS module's debug messages are in
.Pa /proc/spl/kstat/zfs/dbgmsg ,
readable only by root and rewritten whole rather than appended to, so
promtail cannot follow it.
.Nm
appends to
.Pa /var/log/kldload/zfs-dbgmsg.log
the messages newer than the last one it copied, which Loki then shows on
the ZFS dashboard.
Past 50 MB the log is moved to
.Pa zfs-dbgmsg.log.1
and a new one begun.
.Pa kldload-zfs-dbgmsg.timer
runs it 15 seconds after boot and ten seconds after each run ends.
Without the ZFS module it does nothing.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0, copying nothing.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/zfs-dbgmsg.log , Pa .1
The copy, mode 0644.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/.zfs-dbgmsg.lastts
The time of the last message copied.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr arcstats-exporter 8 ,
.Xr zpool-scrub-exporter 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-05 it spent 89 seconds of processor a run on a ten-second
timer, and a line that began with a long number once became the
last-copied time, after which nothing was copied for 22 hours.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: the log was never rotated and had
reached 81 MB.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
